.\" t460: unlace-ir(5) man page — IR format reference
.TH UNLACE-IR 5 "2025-05-13" "unlace 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
unlace-ir \- unlace intermediate representation format
.SH DESCRIPTION
The unlace IR is a register-transfer-level representation with ~70 opcodes.
Each function is represented as a control-flow graph of basic blocks, where
each block contains a sequence of IR instructions.
.SH IR INSTRUCTION FORMAT
Each instruction has the form:
.PP
.RS
.nf
output:type = OPCODE input1, input2, ...
.fi
.RE
.PP
Where:
.TP
.I output
An SSA variable (e.g., \fBv0\fR, \fBv1\fR) with a size annotation.
.TP
.I type
The size in bits: \fBi8\fR, \fBi16\fR, \fBi32\fR, \fBi64\fR, \fBf32\fR, \fBf64\fR.
.TP
.I OPCODE
One of the ~70 IR opcodes (see OPCODES section).
.TP
.I inputs
Zero or more operands: SSA variables or constants.
.SH OPCODES
.SS "Arithmetic"
INT_ADD, INT_SUB, INT_MULT, INT_DIV, INT_SDIV, INT_REM, INT_SREM
.SS "Bitwise"
INT_AND, INT_OR, INT_XOR, INT_NEGATE, INT_LEFT, INT_RIGHT, INT_SRIGHT
.SS "Comparison"
INT_EQUAL, INT_NOTEQUAL, INT_LESS, INT_SLESS, INT_LESSEQUAL, INT_SLESSEQUAL
.SS "Conversion"
INT_ZEXT, INT_SEXT, TRUNC, INT2FLOAT, FLOAT2INT, FLOAT2FLOAT
.SS "Memory"
LOAD, STORE, COPY
.SS "Control Flow"
BRANCH, CBRANCH, BRANCHIND, CALL, CALLIND, RETURN
.SS "Floating Point"
FLOAT_ADD, FLOAT_SUB, FLOAT_MULT, FLOAT_DIV, FLOAT_NEG, FLOAT_ABS,
FLOAT_SQRT, FLOAT_EQUAL, FLOAT_NOTEQUAL, FLOAT_LESS, FLOAT_LESSEQUAL
.SS "Special"
PIECE, SUBPIECE, POPCOUNT, LZCOUNT, BOOL_AND, BOOL_OR, BOOL_NEGATE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unlace (1)
